        "faq_1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is a tea infuser kettle?",
            "answer": "<p>A tea infuser kettle is an electric kettle with a removable stainless-steel basket that sits inside the pot, so you can boil water and steep loose-leaf or bagged tea in the same vessel. When the tea has brewed to your taste, you simply lift the basket out — no separate teapot or strainer needed. Chefman's tea infuser kettles pair this with a fast 1500W boil and a glass body so you can watch the water heat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use both loose-leaf tea and tea bags in the infuser?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The removable stainless-steel infuser basket holds loose-leaf tea for full-flavored brewing, and it works just as well with tea bags when that's what you have on hand. Because the basket lifts right out, you can steep to your preferred strength and remove the leaves before the tea turns bitter.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What sizes do Chefman tea infuser kettles come in?",
            "answer": "<p>Chefman offers tea infuser kettles in 1L, 1.2L, 1.7L, and 1.8L. The 1L is a compact, travel-friendly pick for one or two cups, while the 1.7L and 1.8L brew a full pot to share — a good fit for households or entertaining.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I brew green or white tea in a tea infuser kettle?",
            "answer": "<p>You can, with a small adjustment. Tea infuser kettles are Fast-Boil models that heat to a full 212°F, which is perfect for black and herbal teas. Delicate green, white, and oolong teas taste best below the boil, so let the water cool briefly off the boil before steeping — or choose a Chefman temperature-control kettle that lets you dial in an exact, lower temperature.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I clean a tea infuser kettle?",
            "answer": "<p>Hand-wash the kettle body and the infuser basket, and never submerge the electrical base. If you have hard water, descale about once a month by boiling a 50/50 mix of water and white vinegar, letting it sit for 15 to 20 minutes, then rinsing well. This keeps boil times fast and your water tasting fresh.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are Chefman tea infuser kettles safe to use?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Every Chefman kettle has automatic shut-off and boil-dry protection, lifts off a 360° cordless swivel base, and features a cool-touch handle. All models are cETL approved and backed by a 1-year Chefman assurance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_7": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which Chefman tea infuser kettle is best for me?",
            "answer": "<p>If you mostly brew for yourself or want something travel-friendly, the 1L Tea Infuser Kettle is a compact, top-rated favorite loved by thousands of tea drinkers. If you brew for a household or guests, step up to the 1.7L or 1.8L for a full pot in one go. All of them share the same removable stainless-steel infuser, 1500W fast boil, and see-through glass body.</p>"
          }
        }
